# Modelfile: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, 128K context variant (Legion 5 Pro, 8GB VRAM/32GB RAM)
#
# NOT CURRENTLY BUILT — kept only as a template. Deleted from `ollama list`
# during the ctx16k/32k/64k/128k model-set cleanup (2026-09-12) since it
# lacks the "-safe" treatment (num_predict cap + graceful-output SYSTEM
# prompt) applied to 32k-standalone/64k-agentic, and has no confirmed use case
# yet. If you need it later (e.g. a large-document/RAG task), copy the
# num_predict + SYSTEM block from qwen3.6__35b-a3b-64k-agentic/Modelfile
# (scale num_predict proportionally, e.g. 32768 for a 128K window) before
# running build-model.sh.
#
# Per tuning-results.md, 131072 ctx measured peak ~91% RAM (delta +2.13GB
# over the 8K floor) on Windows — past the 64K "comfortable" inflection
# point but not yet the 256K danger zone. Needs its own verification pass
# on this Ubuntu host (see tuning-results.md follow-up log for results).
#
# Lower num_batch vs the smaller variants to reduce peak memory during
# prompt ingestion, trading a bit of prompt-processing speed for headroom.

FROM qwen3.6:35b-a3b

PARAMETER num_ctx 131072
# num_gpu intentionally omitted — see qwen3.6__35b-a3b-32k-standalone/Modelfile for why
# (host-wide OLLAMA_NUM_GPU/OLLAMA_MAX_VRAM env vars handle offload instead).
PARAMETER num_batch 128
PARAMETER num_thread 16

PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
